cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this data or viewer, please cite the accompanying article
  (see preferred-citation below).
title: >-
  OS Hardening Evaluation — supplementary data, viewer and scoring
  implementation for a comparative quantitative evaluation of kernel
  hardening mechanisms
abstract: >-
  Evaluation data, a static viewer and a reference implementation that
  recomputes every published score, covering 76 kernel hardening mechanisms
  across nine operating systems (Linux, OpenBSD, NetBSD, Fuchsia, GNU/Hurd,
  Redox OS, Zephyr RTOS, Tock OS, seL4) on five dimensions — presence, default
  posture, strength, integration depth and maturity — with per-mechanism
  rationale and upstream commit evidence.
